NOTE:
<a> replace stack with fifoqueue and you have bfs. notice that parent gets processed before its immediate children so its still inorder
but because the while loop is parallel left right ordering cannot be guaranteed

<b> Stack is not really a single stack but implement a special striped stack such that pushes are striped across several. Ideally 
we want dedicated threads sleeping on individual stacks and the goal is to minimize lock contention.



--- Heres a version that does not require pushing the entire tree onto the stack ----

push(root, 0)

while (!empty()) {
  n = pop();
  if (n.index == 0) {
     visit(n.node);
  } 

  if (n.index != n.node.numchildren()) { 
     /* Push the same node back again with a higher index */
     push(n.node, n.index + 1);

     /* All new nodes being discovered for the first time are pushed with an index of 0
      * just like we did for the root node
      */
     push(n.node.children(n.index), 0);
  }
}

